WEBVTT

00:00:00.637 --> 00:00:04.970
Tutorial two. Variables, refraction and visual acuity.

00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:23.382
Files often mix plus and minus cylinder. List each sphere, cylinder and axis set, and the tables use minus cylinder. The astigmatism vectors read the sign of each row's own cylinder, so either form gives the same vector.

00:00:23.561 --> 00:00:31.981
Next, say which notation your visual acuity uses: decimal, logMAR, Snellen, or ETDRS letters.

00:00:32.201 --> 00:00:43.685
Acuity is analyzed in logMAR by default. A table cell then shows the Snellen geometric mean, with the logMAR mean and standard deviation beside it, and the range in Snellen.

00:00:43.922 --> 00:00:56.567
Give each variable a section and a statistical type. The type decides the summary and the test. When patients have two analyzed eyes, the P value is clustered by patient, and each test is named in the output.

00:00:56.744 --> 00:01:01.496
Set the row order of your tables, so they read like the table in your manuscript.

00:01:04.009 --> 00:01:11.732
Variables recorded once per person, such as age and sex, are listed here. They are counted per patient, not per eye.

00:01:12.515 --> 00:01:16.988
StandardEyes. For ophthalmologists, by ophthalmologists.

